# Fixed defect 2438, 2026-11-10, lane b30-pkg: `use <core>`, a package named
# with no module, and no catalogue beside this file (panel 244's critic).
#
# SYMPTOM: `package_wants_a_module`, *`use <core>/parse`, `parse` being a
# file of the package `core`*, a false message: no package `core` is here,
# and core 0.2.1's root holds `strconv`, `strings` and `encoding/`, no
# `parse`.
#
# CAUSE: the parser reads no catalogue and no tree, and its message named a
# module anyway, the same word for every package.
#
# FIX: the parser says how the line goes on, the mark then a module's path,
# naming no module; the parse stage names the modules at the package's root
# where its tree can be read (the folder cases
# `fixedbugs-2438-a-package-named-with-no-module-is-offered-its-modules`),
# and here, with no catalogue and so no tree, nothing is invented.
use <core>  #~ package_wants_a_module

function main()
    print("x")
